meta {
  name: Upsert Channel Override
  type: http
  seq: 12
}

put {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/communication/channel-settings/overrides
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  content-type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "feature": "lab_order_report_published_inform_patient",
    "channel": "WHATSAPP",
    "status": "DONT_SEND"
  }
}

docs {
  Upsert one per-(feature, channel) override for the active scope. `DONT_SEND`
  suppresses that channel for that feature only; `ACTIVE` restores the default.
  Tenant + branch come from the JWT — never the body (CLAUDE.md §4.7).

  This is the business-override gate the notification enablement resolver applies
  after the channel capability gate and before patient opt-out. Returns the full
  settings view (same shape as **Get Channel Settings**).

  ## Fields
  - `feature` (required): a FEATURE_TYPES key.
  - `channel` (required): `EMAIL` | `SMS` | `WHATSAPP` (in-app IAM isn't gated here).
  - `status` (required): `ACTIVE` | `DONT_SEND`.
}
